# The dirty-state scene: unsaved work as window chrome
# (docs/dirty-plan.md). The app declares STATE — one boolean beside
# title and veto_close — and each backend spells its own platform's
# affordance: the dot in the close button on macOS, a leading `*` in
# the rendered caption on Windows, a bullet in the GTK header bar,
# nothing on the phones, which have none. expect_dirty asks the same
# question everywhere and each backend answers it from its own surface
# (D5); one script, five chromes.
#
# THE TITLE IS ASSERTED ONLY WHILE CLEAN, and that is deliberate rather
# than tidiness: the declared string is untouched by this prop on every
# platform (D1 — a marker composed into the app's own title is the
# rejected Qt design), but the WinUI arm composes its asterisk into the
# RENDERED caption, which is exactly what expect_title reads there. An
# expect_title inside the dirty stretch would therefore be a byte
# comparison that cannot hold on all five lanes at once. Assert it here,
# clean, where every backend agrees.
expect label#0 "notes"
expect label#1 "saved"
expect_title "dirty"
expect_dirty false
# An edit changes the model AND declares the window dirty — the
# composition this scene exists to show. Neither implies the other:
# kaya does not watch your signals for you, and dirty is not a
# side effect of writing one.
click button#0
expect label#0 "notes and a line"
expect label#1 "unsaved"
expect_dirty true
# Saving clears both, so the mark comes DOWN as well as up — half a
# lowering that only ever sets the flag passes every assertion above.
click button#1
expect label#1 "saved"
expect_dirty false
# Dirty again, and now the D3 demonstration: the prop arms NOTHING.
# The close attempt fires the veto class (close_requested), the app
# opens its own dialog through the machinery that already exists, and
# cancelling keeps the window — with the mark still up, because
# answering a dialog is not saving.
click button#0
expect label#1 "unsaved"
expect_dirty true
close_window window#0
expect_alert "unsaved changes"
alert_choose cancel
expect label#1 "kept editing"
expect_windows 1
expect_dirty true
